<title>BELGIUM: Belgian bankruptcies down 11.2 pct in September.</title>
<headline>Belgian bankruptcies down 11.2 pct in September.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Company bankruptcies in Belgium fell by 11.2 percent to 606 in September compared with September 1995, Belgian trade and company data group Infotrade said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>In the first nine months of 1996 a total of 5,310 companies went bankrupt, up 4.5 percent from the same 1995 period.</p>
<p>Infotrade said 1,400 jobs had been lost in September as a result of the bankruptcies and about 1.5 billion Belgian francs worth of capital destroyed.</p>
